{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0122 adopted `vector` — a digest of each ticket, embedded and cosine-ranked — as the only candidate distinguishably beating the lexical tier at k=5 (semantic recall@5 0.876 vs 0.823). rebar runs against diverse providers, so this tier must not be reachable through one vendor only, and an installation with no provider must still get surfacing.\n\n## Constraints\n\n**Portability comes from the lexical tier, not this one.** The index sibling [rebar:47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88] ships retrieval and the surfacing sibling [rebar:80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5] the advisory, with no provider, credentials or network. This tier is an opt-in ranking upgrade that degrades to lexical whenever a provider is absent or failing; it replaces only the scoring function and adds the digest-and-embed build step. k stays at 5, the scope of ADR 0122's decision.\n\n**Vendor-neutrality uses a seam the runtime ships.** `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 already backs `src/rebar/llm/providers.py`. Its embeddings API (`infer_embedding_model`, `Embedder`, `EmbeddingModel`) dispatches a `provider:model` string in the shape `providers.py` already uses for chat models.\n\n**A missing optional backend is expected, not a defect.** `pydantic-ai-slim` is not in core `dependencies`; it arrives through `[agents]`, and its per-vendor backends carry their own optional groups, raising `ImportError` naming the group when absent — which must degrade exactly like a provider failure. `pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` and `[bedrock]` already sit in the `dev` extra (`pyproject.toml:315`, `:318`), so AC2 fails rather than skips.\n\n**Both model choices are configuration, and both are unset by default.** `[llm] embedding_model` and `[llm] similar_digest_model`, read from `REBAR_LLM_EMBEDDING_MODEL` and `REBAR_LLM_SIMILAR_DIGEST_MODEL`, follow the provider-qualified-string convention of the existing `model` key. Neither ships an active default: with `embedding_model` unset the query is the lexical tier's. `bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` (1,024 dimensions, cosine) and `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` are ADR 0122's measured values, documented as recommended, not applied on a fresh install.\n\n**The edit set two new `[llm]` keys require.** `src/rebar/llm/config.py` declares the fields on `LLMConfig`; `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` resolves them in `_read_llm_core_settings` via `_llm_str` (both re-exported at `config.py:50-52`, spread at `:519`), so each inherits the CLI>env>file>default precedence every existing `[llm]` string key has. `docs/env-vars.md` is GENERATED by `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` and drift-tested (`tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py`, `tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py`), so it is regenerated and committed here. `tests/golden/config_surface.json` is NOT touched: it inventories only `rebar._config_schema._SECTIONS`, which has no `[llm]` section. The mechanism census records an `[llm]` key under its environment name (39 `env_var::REBAR_LLM_*` baseline entries, zero `config_key::` naming `llm`), so each key carries a `# mechanism-ok: env_var …` marker naming this ticket at its definition site.\n\n**Cosine ranking requires full current-key coverage.** Embedding spaces are not comparable across models, so the index's validity key folds the embedding-model identity and the pinned digest-prompt commit in alongside the sibling's freshness key; changing either invalidates the affected entries. An embedding call can fail partway through a build or re-embed, leaving some live entries vectored and some not. rebar cosine-ranks only when EVERY live entry carries a current-key vector, and otherwise degrades, never ranking across a partial corpus or two embedding spaces.\n\n**Degrade** means retrieval returns the lexical tier's whole-corpus results, the create advisory carries them, a diagnostic is emitted and create exits 0.\n\n**Digest step.** The 4-field prompt pinned at `f147e08242f`, input capped at 40,000 characters, per ADR 0122. Recovery: decode the reply as JSON, else YAML; if that yields no top-level object, extract the first balanced JSON or YAML object embedded in the text, stripping any prose preamble; then unwrap a single wrapper key such as `ticket_digest` before reading the 4 fields. A mapping so recovered whose 4 fields are all empty increments `empties` and degrades, no retry — it is otherwise indistinguishable from success. Only a reply from which no object carrying the field names can be recovered at all increments `digest_unparsed` and is retried once; a retry that succeeds counts as a success and leaves `digest_failed` at 0. This routes ADR 0122's three empty-field shapes — a `ticket_digest` wrapper key, YAML instead of JSON, and JSON behind a prose preamble — to `empties`, not to the retry path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `provider:model` string resolves through `infer_embedding_model` and retrieval cosine-ranks the resulting vectors. Test: configure `TestEmbeddingModel`, assert ordering follows cosine similarity.\n- [ ] A model string for two distinct providers resolves to each provider's embedding model. Test: parameterize over `bedrock:` and `openai:`, assert the matching class each time.\n- [ ] No vendor name appears in a conditional in the retrieval or digest path. Test: assert no `_PROVIDER_PREFIXES` literal occurs in the added modules outside a default-value string or docstring.\n- [ ] The digest model resolves from a configured provider-qualified string. Test: configure a non-Bedrock digest string, assert the resolved model matches.\n- [ ] Changing `[llm] embedding_model` invalidates the affected stored vectors. Test: build, reconfigure, assert those entries re-embed rather than reuse.\n- [ ] Changing the pinned digest-prompt commit invalidates the affected stored vectors. Test: build, repin, assert the same.\n- [ ] A query whose live entries do not all carry a current-key vector degrades. Test: fail the provider after N of M tickets; assert the advisory equals the lexical output and nothing is cosine-ranked.\n- [ ] An interrupted re-embed after a model change never ranks across two embedding spaces. Test: change the key, fail the re-embed after a subset, assert lexical results rather than mixed old-key/new-key vectors.\n- [ ] With `[llm] embedding_model` unset, retrieval degrades. Test: assert the advisory matches the lexical output.\n- [ ] Both new keys are unset by default. Test: assert each resolves to `None` from an environment and config file setting neither.\n- [ ] A backend whose optional dependency is absent degrades, its diagnostic naming the missing group. Test: configure a string whose backend raises `ImportError`; assert exit status, advisory and diagnostic.\n- [ ] A provider denial or timeout degrades. Test: parameterize over both failures; assert exit status, advisory and diagnostic.\n- [ ] A digest mapping recovered with every field empty degrades. Test: assert exit status, advisory and diagnostic.\n- [ ] An `empties` counter records every digest reply recovering a mapping with only empty fields. Test: feed the three shapes ADR 0122 records, assert the counter equals 3.\n- [ ] A build completes despite digest replies parsing to empty fields. Test: the same run indexes the remaining tickets.\n- [ ] A digest reply yielding no recoverable mapping is retried once. Test: return unparseable prose once then succeed; assert `digest_unparsed` is 1.\n- [ ] A digest succeeding on retry is recorded as a success. Test: the same run indexes the ticket and leaves `digest_failed` at 0.\n- [ ] rebar's declared dependencies are unchanged. Test: the dependency and optional-dependency lists are untouched in the diff.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is regenerated and committed carrying both new variables. Test: `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py` leaves no diff and the drift tests pass.\n- [ ] `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0, each new mechanism admitted by a marker naming this ticket. Test: run it.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0. Test: run it.\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793614086574905001,"uuid":"3f522476-41e2-47d9-982d-95a1d87e0470"}